  partId: hand_controllers
  displayName: Rotational and Translational Hand Controllers
  shortName: Hand Controllers
  zone: 1
  order: 120
  keySpec: Manual attitude and translation control
  summary: "Two controllers. The rotational one commands attitude \u2014 pitch, yaw
    and roll. The translational one commands movement along three axes, which is
    what you use for the final metres of a docking."
  whyItMatters: 'Orbital motion is counter-intuitive: to catch a target ahead of
    you, you thrust backwards, dropping into a lower and faster orbit. Docking is
    flown on relative motion, not on instinct.'
  narration: {fileID: 0}
